{"id": 25, "ts": 1780182967.165717, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "agent_1", "message": "I remain convinced that **Candidate\u202fB** is our best choice.\u202fWhile Candidate\u202fD shows strong technical traits\u2014excellent concentration, problem\u2011solving ability, and a serious sense of responsibility\u2014his interpersonal profile is troubling. The notes describe D as \u201cregarded as arrogant,\u201d \u201crelatively weak leadership skills,\u201d and, as just confirmed, he is seen as a \u201cknow\u2011it\u2011all\u201d with a \u201chot temper,\u201d all of which raise serious doubts about his crew\u2011cooperation and professional communication. In a long\u2011distance cockpit, such attitudes can undermine CRM and safety. By contrast, Candidate\u202fB\u2019s only crew\u2011cooperation concern is being \u201cgrumpy\u201d and \u201cuncooperative,\u201d which, as we discussed, can be mitigated through targeted training. Moreover, B already demonstrates the critical safety\u2011critical criteria of operational reliability (\u201cvery conscientious\u201d) and stress resilience (\u201chandles stress very well\u201d), plus solid technical competence. Therefore, given the balance of strengths and weaknesses, I keep my provisional vote for **Candidate\u202fB**."}
